From: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] posix: Fix double free after allocation failure in glob (BZ 34993)

GLIBC-SA-2026-0032 / CVE-2026-126765.  No Fix-Commit is on master or on
release/2.44/master.  The advisory was published as b1950826; the code
fix was posted to libc-alpha on 2026-11-11 by Adhemerval Zanella
(Message-ID 20261111182613.4034113-1-adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org).

prefix_array prepends the directory name to each match in place.  If an
allocation fails partway through, it frees the names it has already
replaced but leaves the pointers in the vector.  Both 2.44 callers then
release that vector with globfree, which frees those names again.

Stop freeing on the failure path.  The array keeps the replaced names
and the original ones after them, and the caller frees all of them.
Adapted to 2.44: prefix_array is the same bug at a different line, and
posix/Makefile has no tst-glob-bz34453, so tst-glob-nospace is added
next to tst-glob-bz30635.

Signed-off-by: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
---
 NEWS                     |   2 +
 posix/Makefile           |   1 +
 posix/glob.c             |  11 ++--
 posix/tst-glob-nospace.c | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 posix/tst-glob-nospace.c

diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -96,6 +96,8 @@
     past the destination (CVE-2026-115819)
   [34991] regex: regex: double free after partial realloc failure
     (CVE-2026-100290)
+  [34993] posix: glob: double free after allocation failure while
+    prepending the directory name (CVE-2026-126765)
   [35016] locale: iconv: CP949 decoder reads past the input on an
     illegal KS C 5601 pair (CVE-2026-121757)
 
diff --git a/posix/Makefile b/posix/Makefile
--- a/posix/Makefile
+++ b/posix/Makefile
@@ -291,6 +291,7 @@
   tst-gai_strerror \
   tst-getopt_long1 \
   tst-glob-bz30635 \
+  tst-glob-nospace \
   tst-glob-tilde \
   tst-glob_symlinks \
   tst-gnuglob \
diff --git a/posix/glob.c b/posix/glob.c
--- a/posix/glob.c
+++ b/posix/glob.c
@@ -1227,7 +1227,10 @@
 /* Prepend DIRNAME to each of N members of ARRAY, replacing ARRAY's
    elements in place.  Return nonzero if out of memory, zero if successful.
    A slash is inserted between DIRNAME and each elt of ARRAY,
-   unless DIRNAME is just "/".  Each old element of ARRAY is freed.  */
+   unless DIRNAME is just "/".  Each old element of ARRAY is freed.
+   If out of memory, ARRAY keeps the elements already replaced and the
+   original ones after them, so the caller can free all of them with
+   globfree.  */
 static int
 prefix_array (const char *dirname, char **array, size_t n)
 {
@@ -1260,11 +1263,7 @@
       size_t eltlen = strlen (array[i]) + 1;
       char *new = malloc (dirlen + 1 + eltlen);
       if (new == NULL)
-        {
-          while (i > 0)
-            free (array[--i]);
-          return 1;
-        }
+        return 1;
 
       {
         char *endp = mempcpy (new, dirname, dirlen);
diff --git a/posix/tst-glob-nospace.c b/posix/tst-glob-nospace.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/posix/tst-glob-nospace.c
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+/* Test glob with injected allocation failures (BZ 34993).
+   Copyright (C) 2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
+   This file is part of the GNU C Library.
